KG42.register("rules-24466a3b5a75d63e78fef895",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R006","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Peers may trade locally produced and stored energy within the community. Scope: Community P2P energy product in the STEP market case Condition: STEP case, with both P2P trade and battery storage enabled. Electricity quantities sold and purchased through local P2P trade must remain within the community. Scope: Local P2P quantities sold and purchased in both model stages Condition: P2P trade is enabled. Locally traded electricity can originate only from distributed generation in the P2P market case. Scope: Locally traded electricity in the P2P market case Condition: P2P case, with direct P2P trade enabled and storage not implemented.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Community P2P energy product in the STEP market case | Local P2P quantities sold and purchased in both model stages | Locally traded electricity in the P2P market case","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e38","v141-b-g03-E07"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Peers may trade locally produced and stored energy within the community. Scope: Community P2P energy product in the STEP market case Condition: STEP case, with both P2P trade and battery storage enabled.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e38"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Electricity quantities sold and purchased through local P2P trade must remain within the community. Scope: Local P2P quantities sold and purchased in both model stages Condition: P2P trade is enabled.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e24"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Locally traded electricity can originate only from distributed generation in the P2P market case. Scope: Locally traded electricity in the P2P market case Condition: P2P case, with direct P2P trade enabled and storage not implemented.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e38","v141-b-g03-E07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"market. In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among ec- prosumers and consumers in a com","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this paper, the market design allows P2P trade among prosumers and consumers in a community. Peers can trade locally produced and stored energy at a dynamic, half-hourly varying P2P price. Some prosumers and consumers have own batteries that can be charged with local generation and from the grid (see, e.g., [26])."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"with their fellow peers. To model these P2P interactions, we ap- ces ply a basic transportation mode","equation_id":"Eqs. (6)-(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The community allows prosumers the direct trade of electricity with their fellow peers. To model these P2P interactions, we apply a basic transportation model for the trade of electricity. The following equations hold true for both stages. To this end, the overall quantity sold X^{(t,h,s)} in both stages for each house h ∈ H is defined as the sum of all electricity flows X_{p}^{(t,h→p,s)} from this house h ∈ H to its peers p ∈ H, as specified in Eq. (6). X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{p≠h} X_{p}^{(t,h→p,s)} \\qquad (6)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"168 J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et al. / account a transmission and conversion lo","equation_id":"Eqs. (8)-(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The sold and purchased quantity can, thus, only stay within the community. The sum of sales over all houses needs to equal the purchases as follows: \\sum_{h} \\psi^{P2P} · X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{h} I^{(t,h,s)} \\quad ∀ t ∈ T, s ∈ S. \\qquad (9)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p09-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"As of today, electricity end-users are at the end of the supply era chain in a still predominant top","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Today’s UK market under dynamic pricing – assuming smart metering – serves in this paper as our base case. To identify the value of each of the proposed local market features – P2P trade and battery storage –, three further cases are compared to the base case: We add P2P trade and battery storage possibilities one by one to investigate their sole values to the system. In short, we apply our model to four cases that distinguish by their options of battery storage and P2P trade. The possibility of feeding from the community into the grid is enabled in all cases. We define the following: • The Base case is defined as today’s electricity market under dynamic real-time pricing. It is not possible to directly trade with other peers, and no electricity storage possibilities are deployed within this case. • The BAT market introduces the possibility of battery storage. Direct trade between the peers is disabled. • The P2P market includes the direct P2P trade connection in the community. The possibility of storage is, however, not implemented. • The STEP market offers both battery storage and P2P trade options within the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"among the peers that reduces the need for grid consumption sig- . niﬁcantly. When both P2P trade and","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"13 A P2P purchase is considered as the indirect use of local resources. Locally traded electricity can only originate from DG in a P2P market."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No x is declared. The source text for this product rule expresses permissions and origin/scoping conditions, not product-level decision variables. The P2P sale/purchase quantities X and I and their balance in Eq. (9) are defined in the clearing section and are owned by v141-c-R001; importing them here would change rule ownership.","empty_theta_reason":"No theta is declared. This product-scope rule has no fixed coefficient, price, efficiency, or numeric input of its own. The P2P efficiency psi^P2P and other constants appear in the clearing/execution rules (R001/R009), not as parameters of product.local_energy."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","quote":"Peers can trade locally produced and stored energy at a dynamic, half-hourly varying P2P price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","quote":"The STEP market offers both battery storage and P2P trade options within the community."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","quote":"The sold and purchased quantity can, thus, only stay within the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"To model these P2P interactions, we apply a basic transportation model for the trade of electricity. The following equations hold true for both stages."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E07","quote":"Locally traded electricity can only originate from DG in a P2P market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e38","quote":"The P2P market includes the direct P2P trade connection in the community. The possibility of storage is, however, not implemented."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2870ab773cf0d94b529509117e93cd6ee175e7a1764c409363344196ee7de9c9","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen R006 graph contains only product.local_energy and no edges. The supplied source statements define a local-energy product scope/permission: peers may trade locally produced and stored energy in the STEP case; local P2P sale/purchase quantities stay within the community; and, in the P2P case, locally traded electricity can originate only from DG. These are procedural product-scope conditions. The quantitative P2P flow definitions and community balance (Eqs. 6-9) are the clearing mathematics assigned by C.1 to R001 (clearing.local), not a product-defining equation for R006. With the frozen graph, no x/theta can be added without either inventing domains/values or duplicating R001's clearing variables. B evidence is UNREVIEWED; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Binds the STEP-case product permission to product.local_energy; no edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Binds the community-containment scope condition to product.local_energy; the quantitative Eq. (9) is not attached because it belongs to R001's clearing node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Binds the DG-origin restriction on locally traded electricity to product.local_energy; no P2P flow node or edge exists in R006."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm that C002's community-containment sentence is intentionally a product-scope condition rather than the Eq. (9) clearing balance already assigned to v141-c-R001. If Eq. (9) must be formalized under R006, C.1 must first add P2P sale/purchase quantity variables, a psi^P2P parameter, and an explicit relation to clearing.local or a matching/execution node; the current frozen graph does not support this without duplicating R001."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
